    {
      "op": "note",
      "text": "Branch of ncr.actions.json: its steps are copied up to the briefing's end (VMQ03a 20, the vertibird called in). Instead of walking out to the pad, the player leaves the dam (travel stand-in: to the Strip). VMQ03aQuestScript fails the quest (120) when the player is outside the HooverDam cells while its timer flag (bQuestTimerActive) is set."
    },
    {
      "op": "note",
      "text": "NCR main-quest chain after the Strip: Things That Go Boom (VMS23), Kings' Gambit (VMS29), For the Republic Part 2 (VMQ05) with You'll Know It When It Happens (VMQ03a, VMQ03aTimer, VHDKimballSpeech, VHDAssassinationDialog), then Eureka! (vHDBattleController) to stage 30. Path: Boomers won over, the King persuaded with his favour, Khans allied, Omerta bosses killed, Mr. House unplugged at his terminal, the Brotherhood allied through Elder McNamara, Kimball kept alive by killing the roof sniper, Legate Lanius talked into leaving. Lines are said with say_info (conditions honoured); no set_stage and no forced line anywhere."
    },
    {
      "op": "note",
      "text": "Given (side quests only as far as this path needs them): Ring-a-Ding-Ding done and the player has been in the Lucky 38 (VStoryEventVisitsLucky38, a condition of the Strip gate trigger that sends Crocker's messenger); Volare! (VMS15) under way with the plane raised (objective 50 done), so Crocker's Boomer ask is open and Pearl's closing line is available; G.I. Blues (VMS19) done, which leaves the King owing the player a favour (KingFavorState 1); How Little We Know (VMS21) at the point where Cachino has set up the meeting with Big Sal and Nero (objective 64 shown, iBossesReady 2); Hidden Valley's lockdown lifted with McNamara still Elder (LockdownLifted 1, CurrentElder 0)."
    },
